<p>And by ‘them,’ we mean commercials. Seriously, feast your eyes on this video that’s, for some reason, two whole minutes long:</p>
<p><iframe allowfullscreen class="youtube" frameborder="0" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/uoF0E6HGkCs?autohide=1&color=white&showinfo=0&theme=light"></iframe></p>
<p>And yes, that’s only eleven years old, but doesn’t it feel like it’s straight out of the 90s?</p>
<p>Anyway, the design options shown may vary from the ones we’re offering today, but you get the point. They’re sheets you put on your kid’s bed that…</p>
<p>Deep singing voice: <em>ZIP, ZIP, ZIP, ZIPPPP!</em></p>
<p>(Is it stuck in your head too?)</p>
<p>In other words, they turn a bed into a sleeping bag and a silly costume all at once, while allowing your child to make their bed easily. You have to admit, it’s sorta neat. And actually it looks cozy as all heck.</p>
<p>In fact, we feel confident saying that, with these ZippySacks, your kiddo will get a great night’s rest… as long as they don’t watch something too spooky before bedtime.</p>
<p>We mention this because the weeks leading up to Halloween are when channels and streaming platforms load up on horror movies for the scare-seekers out there. And some of them? Well, their titles can sound like they’re for kids when, in actuality, they’re chilling tales of terror.</p>
